    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Add two more tests for skipping to skip-failing-curses-tests.patch

- Update to Python 3.16.0a2:
  - Security
    - CVE 2026-115791, gh-161705: Remove sys.path[0] in gzip,
      tarfile and zipfile command line interface to prevent
      shadowing standard library modules from extracted files.
      Issue reported by Jelle Zijlstra, patch by Gregory P. Smith
      and Victor Stinner.
    - CVE 2026-124249, gh-161569: Fix http.cookiejar.CookieJar
      deleting a stored cookie when a response from an unrelated
      host sets an already expired cookie with a Domain or Path
      attribute pointing at that cookie. The cookie policy is now
      consulted before an expired cookie is allowed to delete an
      existing one.
    - CVE 2026-19552, gh-161503: ssl.get_server_certificate() now
      verifies that the server hostname matches its certificate
      when the caller specifies ca_certs.
    - gh-161192: Update bundled libexpat to version 2.10.0 for
      the fixes to CVE 2026-113351, CVE 2026-115506, CVE
      2026-117610 and CVE 2026-118370.
    - CVE 2026-116566, gh-160898: socket.getaddrinfo() now
      rejects null bytes within host and port parameters as this
      previously caused the values to be silently truncated.
      (bsc#1289106)
    - CVE 2026-115559, gh-160369: imaplib.IMAP4.starttls() now
      rejects unexpected plaintext buffered after the STARTTLS
      response, preventing it from being processed as
      TLS-protected data.
    - gh-160279: Prevent venv from importing modules from the</comment>
